Pete.Deglopper@launchpad.unc.edu (Pete Deglopper) writes:
: Well, I was watching my Vorpal Blade behead some nasties the other day,
: and I got to thinking - "He left it dead, and with its head/ He went
: galumphing back."  Perhaps when the VB beheads it could leave a head as a
: trophy, which could then be taken and sacrificed?  It'd be a lot lighter
: than the regular corpse, and probably non-rotting, although also not-edible.
: 

This is the best idea for a Nethack modification I have ever seen posted
here. The Vorpal sword is nice as is, but I think there is still an imbalance
between it and other artifacts (Excalibur, Stormbringer) and that making
this one just a little bit nicer would not do the game any harm.

There should be some monsters that don't leave a head of course, but
I think that's already taken care of in the code, no? Maybe the head could
be useful as a scare monster device - If you have just beheaded an orc,
and another orc appears, and you #apply the head he will be scared off
for some small time. It wouldn't work on six orcs though, they would
get angry and attack straight away. Maybe something like 

result = level of player - (level of monster * number of monsters of type)

where a positive result makes them scared, and they run off for some time
proportional to the result. A positive result just makes them angry, for
ever, until one of you is dead :-). It's not a seriously useful action,
but it could save a life some time. 

